# Day 28/60 — AI Hospital Admission Readiness Simulator

## Objective

Today I built an AI-powered Hospital Admission Readiness Simulator that evaluates whether a patient is fully prepared for hospital admission.

The simulator analyzes documentation, insurance approvals, physician information, bed availability, and clinical readiness while providing an overall admission readiness score.

---

## What Was Generated

- AI Hospital Admission Readiness Simulator
- Admission Workflow Dashboard
- Documentation Readiness Checker
- Insurance & Prior Authorization Validation
- Bed Availability Monitor
- Admission Readiness Score
- Clinical Risk Analysis
- Final Admission Decision Engine

---

## What I Learned

### Hospital Admissions Require Multiple Checks

Patient admission depends on much more than medical diagnosis. Administrative, financial, and clinical factors all influence the final decision.

### Early Risk Detection Saves Time

Identifying missing documents, pending authorizations, or resource shortages early helps reduce delays and improves operational efficiency.

### AI Simplifies Complex Processes

AI can organize large healthcare workflows into interactive dashboards that make decision-making faster and more transparent.

### Better Visualization Improves Understanding

Displaying readiness scores and workflow status gives healthcare professionals a clear picture of admission progress.

